  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "He flies carefully through immemorial white heaven toward Fire Plain grotto-heaven after an ant plague method hits his body and his grotto-heaven. Fire beard grassland and local fire beasts have been ruined, and Righteous Qi Alliance rules force him to spend contribution points, resources, or true inheritances to salvage the disaster. He judges Fang Yuan will keep hunting two-heavens grotto-heavens and that Fire Plain is on that list.",
      "chapters": [
        2106
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_fire_plain_grotto_heaven",
        "fac_righteous_qi_alliance",
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A blue-fog battlefield traps him. Blue-eyed children steal a fire path Immortal Gu from his aperture, and Fang Yuan appears to demand Immortal Gu and Fire Plain grotto-heaven. Fire Plain Grotto Lord activates Furious Red Heart Flames, threatens to burn his Gu and resources, then burns himself to a crisp when the children keep attacking.",
      "chapters": [
        2106
      ],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "ambush-and-death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_immortal_gu",
        "move_furious_red_heart_flames"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan tosses Fire Plain Grotto Lord’s immortal aperture into the sky and later notes that although Fire Plain Grotto Lord was an ordinary rank eight, Fang Yuan only managed to steal one rank eight Immortal Gu from him, with dao marks and defensive killer moves limiting the take.",
      "chapters": [
        2107
      ],
